 "notes": [
  "Oracle IRM = |Ydir|^2 / (|Ydir|^2 + |Ymix - Ydir|^2); the denominator contains late reverberation and babble, so it is a direct-path dominance mask rather than a speech-versus-noise mask.",
  "Oracle masks are built from the simulated direct-path signal and are not available to a real system; the numbers are upper bounds, not achievable accuracy.",
  "All microphones of the array are used. The DOA search covers the front half-plane [-90, 90] deg with a 1 deg step.",
  "One RNG drives the whole run (target direction, target offset, babble windows), so results depend on n_utt and on the condition order."
 ]
